# Draft: kosmickrisp: take flat varyings from the last vertex with a GS
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45938 state=closed
# With `VK_EXT_provoking_vertex` set to last, a KosmicKrisp pipeline with a geometry shader shades flat varyings from the first vertex of each primitive, since Metal always provokes with the first vertex and only the no-GS path (which unrolls the draw) corrects the order.

**Fix:** `poly_nir_lower_gs` gains an `emulate_flatshade_last` mode. In the GS rasterization shader, each vertex also selects the outputs of the last vertex of the line or triangle it starts in its strip, and forwards those for the flat slots (`poly_geometry_params::flat_outputs`, uploaded by kk from the fragment shader's non-interpolated inputs) when the draw's provoking vertex is last. Transform feedback keeps the vertex's own outputs. hk and agx pass `false`; the no-GS path is unchanged.

**Testing** (M4 Pro, macOS 27, CTS 1.4.3.2, debugoptimized, Metal validation with the warning mode):

- A standalone test drawing one triangle and a 6-vertex strip through a GS with flat colors, provoking first and last, with the Vulkan validation layer clean: main takes vertex 0 of each triangle in both modes; this branch takes vertex `i` in first mode and `i + 2` in last mode.
- `dEQP-VK.geometry.*` and `dEQP-VK.rasterization.provoking_vertex.*` from the must-pass list (261 cases): 216 pass, 45 skip on main and on this branch, identical per case. The provoking_vertex cases use no GS, so CTS does not cover this.
- 14,328 further must-pass cases mentioning geometry shaders (pipeline, glsl, draw, rasterization, clipping, spirv_assembly, tessellation): no per-case difference besides `spirv_assembly.*_geom` cases that hit `VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST` under 8 parallel jobs on main as well.
